+// that matches such a step cannot pass through any further sibling steps, so
+// the trailing anchor applies to the matched node unconditionally. Steps that
+// are followed by optional siblings are not marked: whether the anchor applies
+// to them depends on whether those siblings match, which is decided while the
+// query runs (see `list_has_trailing_anchor`).
